{
  "profile": "report",
  "profile_page": "profiles/report.md",
  "notes": [
    "pair: narrative + supertype Report, each trimmed and folded like the room profile's pairs; a report carries the pair and the mark. board_pair: a board entry, the room profile's pair narrative + Board; every board entry here carries the mark too.",
    "mark: x_room_of, read by presence as the room profile reads it. Every room element in the cases carries the world id below; a Narrative with supertype Report and no mark is lore and no report.",
    "thread_cases: each case is the narratives as one reader is given them, in the order given, and a want of three parts, worked by hand from the page's rule 9.",
    "Only reports are in the want: a Narrative that is no report (a message that answers one, a board entry, a lore Narrative) may be among the narratives and is in no part of it.",
    "parents: for each report in the case, in the order given, what its parent is: none (no parent: the field absent, null, not a string or empty once trimmed (of White_Space); a parent with anything left after the trim is read as written), report, board, missing (an id whose element the case does not hold), other (a Narrative that is neither a report nor a board entry) or self. Of these, board is the only kind that is a talk's anchor: a report as a parent never is.",
    "groups: each {parent, kind, reports}: the parent's id, report or board, and the ids of the reports that name it, ordered by created_at as the message profile orders messages (read in the one form the message profile gives, as an instant, a time with no offset as UTC; two at the same instant keep the order given; one that cannot be read after every one that can, in the order given). The parent itself is not in reports. A report in no group and heading none is not listed.",
    "lints: each {kind, report}: chain on a report whose parent is a report that itself has a report for its parent (one the reader holds, the pair and the mark, its own parent read by this rule); self on a report that names itself. A report that names itself is read as naming no parent, so a report that names it is no chain. These are the only lints: a parent that is missing or of no kind is no lint.",
    "The page rules the order inside a group and none between groups: groups and lints each compare as a set. Here groups are listed in the order their parent is first named in the list given, and lints in the order of their reports.",
    "A case's note is prose for the reader of the fixture, never an input."
  ],
